1
US Bank / City of Cheyenne, WY

Collateral Assignment of Construction Documents

and Development Items
12187-0018/LEGAL28035045.2
COLLATERAL ASSIGNMENT OF CONSTRUCTION DOCUMENTS AND
DEVELOPMENT ITEMS

THIS COLLATERAL ASSIGNMENT OF CONSTRUCTION DOCUMENTS AND
DEVELOPMENT ITEMS (the “Assignment”) is given as of November 18, 2013 by CITY OF
CHEYENNE, WYOMING a municipal corporation duly organized and existing under the
Constitution of the State of Wyoming ("City") to U.S. BANK NATIONAL ASSOCIATION, a
national banking association, its successors and assigns ("Bank").
RECITALS:

A.
City has executed a Purchase Agreement of even date (the "PSA") evidencing the
purchase of certain property and improvements that will be improved ("Project") which is
located upon that certain real property more particularly described on Exhibit A, attached hereto
and made a part hereof by this reference ("Land").  Capitalized terms not otherwise defined
herein shall have the meaning given to them in the PSA (as it may be amended, restated,
extended, renewed, or otherwise modified from time to time).
B.
The Bank has required the execution of this Assignment as a condition to Bank's
purchase of the Project and payment of the Acquisition Price as described in the PSA, and the
Bank would not purchase the Project or advance the Acquisition Price on the same terms and
conditions without this Assignment.
ASSIGNMENT

FOR VALUE RECEIVED, the receipt and sufficiency of which is hereby acknowledged,
and as part of the consideration for the purchase of the Project, City and Bank agree as follows:
1.
Assignment.  City does hereby assign to Bank, its successors and assigns, the non-
exclusive use of all of City’s right, title and interest in and to the Construction Documents
(defined in the PSA) and the following items of personal property (the “Development Items”)
now or hereafter used or useful in connection with the development and construction of the
Improvements;
(a)
All plans and specifications prepared for the construction of any
improvements, including without limitation, all studies, estimates, data, drawings, trade names,
trademarks, and service marks;
(b)
All contracts, agreements, rights, documents, or instruments arising out of
or in connection with the Project and the construction of the Improvements, whether now or
hereafter existing;
(c)
All documents, instruments and agreements relating to, or in any way
connected with, the operation, control, development or construction of the Improvements,
including without limitation, any declaration of covenants, conditions and restrictions and any
articles of incorporation, bylaws and other membership documents of any property owners
```

