PSA), subcontracts, agreements with suppliers of material, management contracts, service
contracts, maintenance contracts, franchise agreements, license agreements, building permits and
operating licenses with respect to the Project.
2.
Revocable License.
The Bank hereby grants to City a license to use the
Development Items prior to the occurrence of any Event of Default (defined in the PSA) under
the PSA or Lease.  Such license shall be revocable by Bank without notice to City at any time
upon or after an Event of Default under the PSA or Lease, and immediately upon any such
revocation, the Bank shall be entitled to receive and use the Development Items.
3.
Representations and Warranties of City.
City represents and warrants that:
(a)
The Development Items are held by City or when acquired by City will be
held by City free and clear of all liens, security interests and charges and the Development Items
have not been pledged as collateral for any obligations other than the assignment contained in
this Assignment.  The City covenants and agrees with Bank to perform all acts required of it to
maintain the Development Items in good standing at all times.
(b)
The Plans (and other relevant Development Items) for the Improvements
covered by each building permit have been or will be approved by all governmental authorities
whose approval is required or appropriate at the time such permit is issued.  The Plans are those
which are to be used in the actual construction of the Improvements described therein.
(c)
City has not conveyed, transferred, or assigned the Development Items or
any right or interest therein and has not executed any other document or instrument that might
prevent or limit the Bank from operating under the terms, conditions and provisions of this
Assignment.
(d)
City shall make no other assignment of the Development Items or of any
right or interest therein.
(e)
City shall perform and observe, in timely fashion, all of the covenants,
conditions, obligations and agreements of City in connection with the Development Items, in
material accordance with the terms, conditions and provisions thereof.
(f)
City shall not waive, execute any agreement which could be interpreted as
waiving, or in any manner release or discharge any party from, the material covenants,
conditions, obligations or agreements to be performed or observed in connection with the
Development Items, or condone any nonperformance thereof, but shall, at its sole cost and
