### Page 3 of 6

```text
3
US Bank / City of Cheyenne, WY

Collateral Assignment of Construction Documents

and Development Items
12187-0018/LEGAL28035045.2
expense, enforce and secure the performance of all material covenants, conditions, obligations
and agreements to be performed or observed in connection with the Development Items.
4.
Indemnity.  In the exercise of the powers herein granted, no liability shall be
asserted or enforced against the Bank prior to the enforcement of its rights hereunder, all such
liability being hereby expressly waived and released by the City.  City shall and does hereby
agree to pay the Bank as Additional Rent under the Lease all amounts incurred by Bank for
liability, loss or damage which it may or might incur by reason of this Assignment and of and
from any and all claims and demands whatsoever which may be asserted against the Bank by
reason of any alleged obligations or undertakings required to be performed by City in connection
with the rights and privileges hereby assigned, except to the extent caused by the Bank's gross
negligence or willful misconduct.
5.
Bank’s Rights.  Although it is the intention of the parties that this instrument shall
be a present assignment, it is expressly understood and agreed, anything herein contained to the
contrary notwithstanding, that the Bank shall not exercise any of the rights or powers herein
conferred upon it until an Event of Default has occurred under the PSA or Lease, but upon the
occurrence of any such Event of Default, the Bank shall be entitled to all the rights, privileges
and benefits of City, including the right to use the Development Items.
6.
Attorney-In-Fact.  City does hereby make, constitute and appoint Bank, and its
successors and assigns, as City’s true and lawful attorney-in-fact, in City’s name, place and
stead, or otherwise, upon the occurrence of a nonappropriation event under Section 3.3 of the
Lease ("Nonappropriation Event"), any Event of Default, as that term is defined in the PSA or
Lease, and at any time while such Event of Default is continuing:
(a)
To do all acts and to execute, acknowledge, obtain and deliver any and all
instruments, documents, items or things necessary, proper or required in order to use the
Development Items;
(b)
To give any notices, instructions, or other communications in connection
with the Development Items;
(c)
To demand and receive all performances due in connection with the
Development Items and to take all lawful ways and means for the enforcement thereof and to
compromise and settle any claim or cause of action in City arising from or related to the
Development Items and give acquittances and other sufficient discharges relating thereto; and
(d)
To file any claim or proceeding or to take any other action, either in its
own name, in that of its nominee, in the name of City, or otherwise, to enforce the right to use
the Development Items or protect and preserve the right, title and interest of Bank hereunder.
The power of attorney given herein is a power coupled with an interest and shall be
irrevocable so long as any part of the PSA or Lease remains unpaid or unperformed.  Bank shall
have no obligation to exercise any of the foregoing rights and powers in any event.
