### Page 4 of 6

```text
4
US Bank / City of Cheyenne, WY

Collateral Assignment of Construction Documents

and Development Items
12187-0018/LEGAL28035045.2
7.
Bank’s Counsel.  Following a Nonappropriation Event or an Event of Default,
Bank shall have the right at any time to appear in and defend and be represented by counsel of its
own choice in any action or proceeding purporting to affect City’s rights related to the
Development Items.
8.
Additional Indebtedness/Nonappropriation.  All sums advanced or paid by the
Bank under the terms hereof, all amounts paid, suffered or incurred by Bank in exercising any
authority granted herein, including reasonable attorneys’ fees, and all other amounts due the
Bank from City in connection with this Assignment, the PSA or Lease shall be added to the
indebtedness evidenced by the PSA and Lease subject to the non-appropriation provisions in the
PSA and Lease, provided however, a Nonappropriation Event shall not terminate this
Assignment but shall entitle Bank to elect to step into the place of City and continue to make
payments required by the Contract so long as Architect performs, or terminate the Contract, as
determined by Bank.
9.
City Liability.  Neither the execution and delivery of this Assignment nor any
failure on the part of any person preparing the Development Items to comply with, honor and
perform in accordance with any agreements made by that person shall affect the liability of any
party to pay and perform the obligation under the PSA and Lease.
10.
No Release.  The taking of this Assignment by the Bank shall not effect the
release of any other collateral now or hereafter held by Bank as security for the obligations
described in the PSA or Lease, nor shall the taking of additional security for the obligations
described in the PSA or Lease hereafter effect a release or termination of this Assignment or any
terms, conditions or provisions hereof.
11.
Termination.  Upon payment in full of the Purchase Price and all other sums due
if City exercises its option to purchase the Project described in Article 10 of the Lease, this
Assignment shall cease, terminate and be of no further effect; provided, however, that the
affidavit, certificate, letter or statement of the Bank or any officer, agent or attorney of the Bank
showing any part of the Purchase Price or other amounts payable for the exercise being unpaid
shall constitute conclusive evidence of the validity, effectiveness, and continuing force of this
Assignment and any person may, and is hereby authorized to, rely thereon.  City hereby
authorizes and directs all entities having any interest in the Development Items, upon receipt of
written notice from the Bank, to recognize the Bank as entitled to exercise all powers and receive
all benefits of City thereunder.
12.
Further Assurances.  City, upon request of the Bank, shall execute and deliver
such additional documents, including but not limited to financing statements, and do such other
acts as may be reasonably necessary to fully implement the intent of this Assignment and to
perfect and preserve the rights and interests of Bank hereunder and the priority thereof.
13.
Inurement.  Time is of the essence hereof.  This Assignment shall be binding upon
City and its successors and assigns and shall inure to the benefit of Bank and its successors and
assigns.  This Assignment, however, is not intended to confer any right or remedies upon any
person other than the parties hereto and their successors and assigns.
